          equipment: "32 Chinese dominoes, a 'Chung' marker for the banker, and three dice to determine the deal order.",
          dealing: 'Tiles are stacked in a 4x8 woodpile; dice are rolled to select which player receives the first stack.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Arrange four tiles into two pairs that both beat the banker's corresponding pairs according to traditional tile rankings.",
          gameplay: '1. Woodpile: Tiles are shuffled and stacked in a woodpile. 2. Deal: Players receive four tiles based on a dice roll. 3. Partition: Divide tiles into a high hand and a low hand. 4. Ranking: High hand must rank equal to or higher than the low hand. 5. Showdown: Banker compares pairs with each player. 6. Settlement: Win both pairs to win; lose both to lose; split results in a push.',
          keyRules: [
            'The high hand must always be equal to or higher in rank than the low hand partition.',
            "To win the wager, both player pairs must outrank the banker's pairs; one win and one loss is a push.",
            'Ties on a specific pair comparison (copy hands) are won by the banker.',
            'The Luk and Saam tiles known together as Gee Joon are semi-wild and can be used as three or six to optimize hand totals.',
            'The precedence of combinations is as follows: Gee Joon followed by Traditional Bo Pairs then Wongs then Gongs and finally High Nines.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Learn to recognize the matched pairs immediately and understand the mod-10 scoring for non-ranking hands.',
          intermediate: 'Balance the strength between your high and low hands; a very strong high hand often leaves a vulnerable low hand.',
          advanced: "Master the 'House Way' for dealer play and use it as a baseline for your own strategic partitions.",
          tips: [
            'Never split matched pairs unless they can form even stronger individual ranking combinations.',
            'Use the Gee Joon wild tiles to bridge gaps in your modular totals to reach nine.',
            "Track which high-ranking tiles have been played to estimate the banker's remaining strength.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
          nullReasons: {},
        },
